            'eligibility_html' => '<p>For a business purpose, the Embassy of Luxembourg\'s checklist (via VFS, though the specific checklist found was for a related "cultural" visa category using the same general format) requires an invitation letter from the inviting Luxembourg company, university, fair, congress, sport federation, or organiser, stating the purpose of the visit and the complete programme of activities and/or meetings to attend, plus a covering letter on the applicant\'s employer\'s original business letterhead, stating the applicant\'s position, length of service, and confirmation that adequate leave has been granted. Proof of sufficient financial means and a return ticket or reservation are also listed. The tourist-visa checklist for the same embassy additionally lists a passport valid at least 3 months beyond the date of return, with at least 2 blank pages, plus a copy of the passport\'s data page &mdash; this is presumed (but not separately confirmed) to also apply to the business category. A third-party consultancy guide suggests the invitation letter should ideally also include the Luxembourg company\'s registration number (RCS Luxembourg), the exact purpose and duration of the visit, the contact person\'s name and designation, and a statement of who bears the costs of the trip &mdash; this detail could not be confirmed against an official source and should be treated as good practice rather than a confirmed requirement. Compulsory travel medical insurance with cover of at least EUR 30,000 is required.</p><p>For business visas specifically, submission at VFS can reportedly be made by the applicant, an authorised company representative, or a travel agent, unlike tourist applications which must be submitted by the applicant in person.</p>',
