            'intro_html' => '<p>Turkmenistan runs an unusually opaque, invitation-letter-gated visa system, and this was confirmed directly from Turkmenistan embassy (.gov.tm) pages rather than only third-party guides. The process starts with a Letter of Invitation (LOI) issued by the State Migration Service of Turkmenistan (SMST), which must be requested by a counterpart already inside Turkmenistan — for a business trip, this would be the inviting Turkmen company or organisation, not the Indian applicant. Only once the LOI is approved can the applicant submit a standard visa application (form, photo, passport, fee) at a Turkmenistan embassy or consulate, such as the one in New Delhi.</p><p>Timing estimates vary and conflict: one travel-industry source cites an official 12-day LOI processing time but recommends budgeting around 20 days due to frequent delays, while another travel operator estimates 3–4 weeks overall; the embassy pages themselves cite roughly 10 business days for the visa step once the LOI is in hand. One source also notes that LOI applications can now be submitted up to 6 months before travel (extended from 3 months before May 2025), and that the Independence Day period (20–30 September) carries additional quota restrictions — neither of these specifics could be independently corroborated beyond this single travel-industry source.</p>',
