            'eligibility_html' => '<p>Confirmed from official Turkmenistan embassy pages: the LOI must be filed by the inviting counterpart in Turkmenistan (the business host or, for tourism, a licensed Turkmen travel agency — ordinary individuals or companies cannot self-invite for tourism purposes). Once the LOI is approved, the applicant submits it together with a completed visa application form, a passport photo, and a passport valid for at least 6 months from the date of departure, plus the applicable fee.</p><p>Third-party sources, with lower confidence, add that a business covering letter should be on the inviting/host company\'s letterhead with an official seal and signature, stating the applicant\'s and company\'s details and the planned length of stay, and that roughly six months of bank statements may be requested — neither of these two specifics could be confirmed on an official embassy page in this pass.</p>',
